E["npc:cyrus-therepentous"] = {t="npc",n="Cyrus Therepentous",z="burningsteppes",s="At Slither Rock, Cyrus Therepentous puts mortals who enter his lair to the test. He seeks survivors strong enough to serve the Black dragonflight.",h="At Slither Rock, Cyrus Therepentous puts mortals who enter his lair to the test.",sec={{t="The Master of Slither Rock",b="From his cavern at Slither Rock, Cyrus Therepentous watches the volcanic crags of the Burning Steppes. He scorns mortal travelers and calls anyone who disturbs his lair a fool. Yet he does not strike every trespasser down. Instead, he sends his minions against them in a deadly trial. Those who survive the flames may prove useful to the Black dragonflight.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Cyrus Therepentous?",a="Cyrus Therepentous is an intelligent black dragonspawn who serves the Black dragonflight. He tests mortals who enter his cave at Slither Rock in the Burning Steppes.",al={"cyrus therepentous","who is cyrus","slither rock dragonspawn"}},{q="Where can Cyrus Therepentous be found?",a="Cyrus Therepentous dwells deep in a cave at Slither Rock, in the northeastern Burning Steppes.",al={"cyrus location","where is cyrus therepentous","cyrus cave"}},{q="Why doesn't Cyrus attack adventurers on sight?",a="Cyrus Therepentous considers eating trespassers, but first tests whether they might prove useful. He pits them against deadly trials and his minions, sparing those who prove their worth.",al={"why is cyrus friendly","why doesn't cyrus kill me","cyrus talk"}}},kw={"black dragonflight","burning steppes","cyrus therepentous","dragonspawn","slither rock","taste of flame"},rel={"subzone:slither-rock","zone:burningsteppes","topic:black-dragonflight","zone:searinggorge"},src={"Cyrus Therepentous"}}
E["npc:john-j-keeshan"] = {t="npc",n="John J. Keeshan",z="burningsteppes",s="In the Redridge fighting, Corporal John J. Keeshan was taken prisoner by the Blackrock orcs. After the battle around Stonewatch, they dragged him deep into Render's Rock.",h="In the Redridge fighting, Corporal John J.",sec={{t="A Soldier of Redridge",b="Corporal John J. Keeshan serves Stormwind in the Redridge Mountains. He was posted there as Blackrock orcs pressed against Lakeshire and its defenders. When fighting flared around Stonewatch Keep, Keeshan stood with the soldiers holding the line for the kingdom.",sp=0},{t="Captivity at Render's Rock",b="The Blackrock clan pushed north from the Burning Steppes into the Redridge Mountains. Keeshan joined the defenders at Stonewatch Keep, but the orcish assault overwhelmed them. The orcs took him alive and hauled him deep into Render's Rock, where he remained a prisoner behind enemy lines. Alliance rescue parties had to fight their way in to break him out.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is John J. Keeshan?",a="Corporal John J. Keeshan serves in Stormwind's army and fought the Blackrock orcs in the Redridge Mountains. He was captured during the battle around Stonewatch Keep and taken to Render's Rock.",al={"keeshan lore","who is keeshan","corporal keeshan"}},{q="Why is Keeshan imprisoned in Render's Rock?",a="The Blackrock orcs overwhelmed Keeshan during the battle around Stonewatch Keep and took him alive. They hauled him to their encampment inside the caves of Render's Rock.",al={"why is keeshan captured","render's rock prisoner","how did keeshan get captured"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier, Keeshan was taken captive while holding the line for Stormwind against the Blackrock orcs in Redridge.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, Keeshan shows the danger of the Redridge front, where even hardened soldiers can be overwhelmed and carried off by the Blackrock clan."},kw={"john j keeshan","keeshan","missing in action","render's rock","stonewatch"},rel={"quest:219","subzone:render-s-rock","subzone:stonewatch","subzone:stonewatch-keep","zone:redridge","topic:third-war","topic:alliance"},src={"John J. Keeshan"}}
E["npc:marshal-maxwell"] = {t="npc",n="Marshal Maxwell",z="burningsteppes",s="At Morgan's Vigil, Marshal Maxwell holds the northern ridge against the Blackrock clan and Dark Iron dwarves. The Stormwind officer directs scouts through the hostile crags and searches for his captured comrade, Marshal Reginald Windsor.",h="At Morgan's Vigil, Marshal Maxwell holds the northern ridge against the Blackrock clan and Dark Iron dwarves.",sec={{t="A Lonely Post on the Steppes",b="Marshal Maxwell commands Stormwind's detachment at Morgan's Vigil on the southern rim of the Burning Steppes. The outpost overlooks ash, dragonkin, and Blackrock orcs. Travelers crossing the fiery crags find a rare friendly post here.\n\nFrom the rocky ridge, Maxwell directs the defense against mountain threats before they can move south into Redridge and Elwynn.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Truth in the Mountain",b="Marshal Maxwell directs field operations aimed at Blackrock Spire and Blackrock Depths. Reports suggest his captured comrade, Marshal Reginald Windsor, may still be alive in the Dark Iron dwarves' dungeons. Maxwell gathers intelligence and sends trusted champions to attempt a rescue. From Morgan's Vigil, he links frontier scouting with turmoil inside Stormwind's gates.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Marshal Maxwell?",a="Marshal Maxwell is a high-ranking Stormwind officer at Morgan's Vigil in the Burning Steppes. He commands the local Alliance forces watching the Blackrock orcs, Black dragons, and Dark Iron dwarves.",al={"marshal maxwell lore","who is maxwell"}},{q="Why is Marshal Maxwell stationed at Morgan's Vigil?",a="Morgan's Vigil guards the Alliance's northernmost fortified ridge above the Redridge Mountains. Maxwell holds the mountain pass and watches for threats from Blackrock Mountain.",al={"why is maxwell in burning steppes","morgan's vigil commander"}},{q="What is Maxwell's connection to Marshal Windsor?",a="Marshal Maxwell helps lead the search for his captured comrade, Marshal Reginald Windsor, taken to Blackrock Depths. He coordinates rescue efforts and sends vital intelligence about Windsor back to Stormwind.",al={"maxwell and windsor","abandoned hope quest lore"}},{q="Does Marshal Maxwell help organize strikes against Blackrock Spire?",a="Yes. Maxwell directs veteran Alliance champions against the Blackrock clan's leaders and the forces holding Blackrock Spire's heights. His directives target General Drakkisath and his forces.",al={"maxwell drakkisath","maxwell's mission"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion in the Burning Steppes, you find Stormwind's authority in Marshal Maxwell, who leads the campaign against Blackrock Mountain.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you see Stormwind's frontline discipline in Maxwell. He coordinates deep assaults behind enemy lines amid the volcanic ash."},kw={"blackrock depths","burning steppes","general drakkisath","marshal maxwell","maxwell","morgans vigil","reginald windsor","stormwind army"},rel={"subzone:morgan-s-vigil","zone:burningsteppes","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Marshal Maxwell"}}
E["npc:mathredis-firestar"] = {t="npc",n="Mathredis Firestar",z="burningsteppes",s="At Flame Crest, Mathredis Firestar binds Lesser Arcanums in the Burning Steppes. He relies on his dead mentor’s research and the energy released by each binding.",h="At Flame Crest, Mathredis Firestar binds Lesser Arcanums in the Burning Steppes.",sec={{t="A Master's Legacy and Magic Addiction",b="At Flame Crest in the Burning Steppes, Mathredis Firestar crafts Lesser Arcanums from his mentor Telmius Dreamseeker’s work. Telmius died in Dire Maul’s ancient ruins while seeking magical secrets from the Shen'dralar. He invented the bindings, but Mathredis cannot yet make the greatest arcanums. So he turns to lesser ones.\n\nHis craft is more than study. Like other blood elves since the Sunwell fell, Mathredis hungers for arcane power. Binding materials to ancient librams releases violent magical discharges. He draws on that energy to sustain himself.",sp=0},{t="The Art of the Arcanum",b="Mathredis accepts the proper tomes, including the Librams of Constitution, Resilience, Rumination, Tenacity, or Voracity, along with rare reagents. He binds the volatile reagents to the text and concentrates their essence into an arcanum. The finished arcanum permanently enchants headwear or leg armor.\n\nWhen adventurers bring the components, Mathredis trades his craft for payment and the arcane sustenance he craves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mathredis Firestar?",a="Mathredis Firestar is a blood elf mage at Flame Crest, a neutral outpost in the Burning Steppes. He can forge Lesser Arcanums to enchant armor.",al={"mathredis lore","who is mathredis firestar","firestar blood elf"}},{q="Why is Mathredis creating arcanums?",a="Since the Sunwell was destroyed, blood elves have suffered severe magical withdrawal. Mathredis draws on the residual energy released as he creates and binds arcanums to ease his addiction.",al={"why make arcanums","mathredis motivation","why librams"}},{q="Who was Telmius Dreamseeker?",a="Telmius Dreamseeker was Mathredis's late master and the inventor of arcanums. He went to Dire Maul to seek knowledge from the Shen'dralar, but died there before passing on all his expertise.",al={"telmius","mathredis master","who was his master"}},{q="What kinds of arcanums can Mathredis make?",a="Mathredis can forge Lesser Arcanums of Constitution, Resilience, Rumination, Tenacity, and Voracity. His master's most potent arcanums remain beyond his grasp.",al={"which arcanums","lesser arcanums","libram list"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can recognize Mathredis's arcanum craft as a desperate, volatile way to draw raw magical nourishment from the binding process."},kw={"arcanum","burning steppes","dreamseeker","firestar","flame crest","libram","mathredis","telmius"},rel={"subzone:flame-crest","zone:burningsteppes","subzone:dire-maul"},src={"Mathredis Firestar"}}
E["subzone:altar-of-storms-burning-steppes"] = {t="subzone",n="Altar of Storms (Burning Steppes)",z="burningsteppes",s="Blackrock warlocks perform fel rites at the Altar of Storms in the Burning Steppes. The dark monument draws those seeking demonic power.",h="Blackrock warlocks perform fel rites at the Altar of Storms in the Burning Steppes.",sec={{t="A Legacy of Shadow and Flame",b="Blackrock warlocks hold the Altar of Storms, where they perform rites to channel fel magic and seal dark pacts. The monument was built during the earlier wars. Nearby, the hermit Gorzeeki Wildeyes and his master, Mor'zul Bloodbringer, keep an encampment overlooking the altar. Renegade practitioners study its violent energies and devise demanding rites for spellcasters who seek greater dark power.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Altar of Storms?",a="The Altar of Storms is a corrupted stone monument used for fel rites and to channel demonic energy. Built during the Old Horde's wars, it remains a source of dark power for Blackrock warlocks.",al={"altar of storms lore","what is this altar","burning steppes altar"}},{q="Who controls the altar right now?",a="Hostile Blackrock orc warlocks and acolytes occupy the grounds around the altar. They perform dark ceremonies and guard the site from intruders.",al={"who is at altar of storms","altar of storms enemies","who lives here"}},{q="Who is Gorzeeki Wildeyes?",a="Gorzeeki Wildeyes is an eccentric goblin scholar of the dark arts and a hermit on the hill overlooking the altar. He lives there with his master, Mor'zul Bloodbringer, and helps powerful warlocks master greater demonic bindings.",al={"gorzeeki wildeyes","orc on the hill","who is gorzeeki"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can seek the materials and rites for summoning a dreaded dreadsteed from Mor'zul Bloodbringer and Gorzeeki Wildeyes, the hermits near the Altar of Storms.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you may find the altar an uncomfortable reminder of the Old Horde's dark history. Gul'dan's Shadow Council used similar foul shrines to infuse ogres and soldiers with dark sorcery."},kw={"altar of storms","blackrock","burning steppes","fel","gorzeeki wildeyes","mor'zul bloodbringer","warlock"},rel={"zone:burningsteppes","topic:blackrock-clan"},src={"Altar of Storms (Burning Steppes)"}}
E["subzone:blackrock-mountain"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackrock Mountain",z="burningsteppes",s="In Blackrock Mountain, rival armies fight above depths scarred by fire and war. Ragnaros's summoning raised the volcano between the Burning Steppes and the Searing Gorge, and its roots now hold dwarven halls.",h="In Blackrock Mountain, rival armies fight above depths scarred by fire and war.",sec={{t="A Cataclysmic Origin",b="Blackrock Mountain rose from the War of the Three Hammers two and a half centuries ago. The united armies of Ironforge and the Wildhammer clan threatened to destroy the Dark Iron dwarves. So Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan reached into the earth for a weapon, and his spell broke the barriers between worlds. It brought Ragnaros the Firelord to Azeroth.\n\nThe blast tore apart the Redridge range, carved out the Searing Gorge and Burning Steppes, and hurled a vast volcano into the sky. Thaurissan died in the destruction. The surviving Dark Iron clan was bound to serve the Firelord forever. They carved Shadowforge City deep among the mountain's roots.",sp=0},{t="Citadel of Ash and Blood",b="Blackrock Mountain claimed a grim place in history during the First and Second Wars. After Stormwind was sacked, Orgrim Doomhammer purged the Shadow Council and made Blackrock Spire the Horde's fortress capital. The mountain remains a battlefield.\n\nDark Iron dwarves and their elemental master hold the fiery depths. Above, rogue Blackrock orcs, dragonkin, and their dark masters occupy the spires.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How was Blackrock Mountain created?",a="Blackrock Mountain rose about two hundred and fifty years ago during the War of the Three Hammers. Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan sought power beneath the earth to defeat rival dwarven clans. His spell summoned Ragnaros the Firelord and unleashed the blast that raised the volcano.",al={"origin of blackrock mountain","who made blackrock mountain","how did the volcano form"}},{q="Why is it named Blackrock Mountain?",a="No account names the first person to call it Blackrock Mountain. The name also belongs to the Blackrock orcs. During the Second War, Orgrim Doomhammer's Horde made Blackrock Spire its capital, and Blackrock remnants still hold it.",al={"blackrock name origin","named after blackrock clan"}},{q="Who controls Blackrock Mountain right now?",a="Dark Iron dwarves hold the halls of Shadowforge City and serve Ragnaros. Above them, Blackrock remnants and black dragonkin dominate Blackrock Spire.",al={"who lives in blackrock","who rules blackrock mountain"}},{q="What zones connect through Blackrock Mountain?",a="Interior paths and chains through Blackrock Mountain link the Searing Gorge to the north with the Burning Steppes to the south.",al={"how to get through blackrock","blackrock mountain connections"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Blackrock Mountain marks a dark chapter in their history. The Dark Iron clan's folly cost them their freedom and scarred the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Blackrock Spire recalls bondage and bloodshed under Doomhammer. Rogue orcs who reject Thrall's leadership now contest it."},kw={"blackrock mountain","blackrock spire","burning steppes","doomhammer","ragnaros","searing gorge","shadowforge","thaurissan"},rel={"zone:burningsteppes","zone:searinggorge","topic:dark-iron-clan","topic:blackrock-clan","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","topic:shadow-council","topic:second-war","zone:redridge"},src={"Blackrock Mountain"}}
E["subzone:blackrock-pass"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackrock Pass",z="burningsteppes",s="At Blackrock Pass, a heavy iron gate marks the road from Redridge Mountains into the Burning Steppes. The corridor runs north beneath the cliffs, from human heartlands to the war grounds of Dark Iron dwarves and Blackrock orcs. Travelers on foot cross a harsh frontier.",h="At Blackrock Pass, a heavy iron gate marks the road from Redridge Mountains into the Burning Steppes.",sec={{t="A Scorched Threshold",b="Blackrock Pass cuts through the mountains between Redridge Mountains and the Burning Steppes. A heavy iron gate marks the rocky boundary, beyond the forests and lakes of the southern valleys. South of the gate, Lakeshire's beleaguered militia protects pastoral lands. North of it, fire elementals, dragonkin, and hostile orc warbands fill an open wasteland. Few cross on foot unless bound for the shadow of Blackrock Mountain itself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Blackrock Pass lead?",a="Blackrock Pass leads from the northern border of Redridge Mountains into the southern perimeter of the Burning Steppes. It is a direct overland gateway between the southern Alliance territories and the foothills of Blackrock Mountain.",al={"where does blackrock pass go","blackrock pass destination","path from redridge to burning steppes"}},{q="Is it safe for travelers from Lakeshire to cross the pass?",a="No. The lands north of the pass are far more dangerous than the hills around Redridge. Ferocious Blackrock orcs, giant fire elementals, and black whelps make the Burning Steppes hazardous for low-level adventurers and common wayfarers.",al={"can i go through blackrock pass","is blackrock pass dangerous","level requirement blackrock pass"}},{q="Who controls Blackrock Pass?",a="Neither Stormwind nor the Horde holds full control over Blackrock Pass. Blackrock orcs and wild beasts press in on the sparsely fortified chokepoint, while Redridge town guards watch from below with deep dread.",al={"who owns blackrock pass","guards at blackrock pass","faction control blackrock pass"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Redridge's defenders and the Kingdom of Stormwind, Blackrock Pass is a constant source of dread. It offers Blackrock orcs a straight path south into human lands."},kw={"blackrock orcs","blackrock pass","burning steppes","frontier","gate","lakeshire","redridge mountains"},rel={"zone:burningsteppes","zone:redridge","subzone:blackrock-mountain"},src={"Blackrock Pass"}}
E["subzone:blackrock-stronghold"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackrock Stronghold",z="burningsteppes",s="Dark Horde orcs hold the approaches to Blackrock Mountain from Blackrock Stronghold. Their fortified camp is a field garrison in the Burning Steppes.",h="Dark Horde orcs hold the approaches to Blackrock Mountain from Blackrock Stronghold.",sec={{t="Garrison of the Dark Horde",b="Blackrock Stronghold spreads across the scorched foothills below Blackrock Mountain. The Blackrock clan keeps its main base here in the Burning Steppes. These orcs cling to the old ways of war. They follow Rend Blackhand and the dragonkin lurking above in the spire, not Thrall's Horde.",sp=0},{t="Front Line of Blackrock Spire",b="Blackrock Stronghold guards the mountain's southern approaches. Its forces gather for attacks into the Redridge Mountains and neighboring human lands. The watch is constant, and anyone crossing the blasted wastes meets its challenge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Blackrock Stronghold?",a="In the northern Burning Steppes, Blackrock Stronghold guards the approaches to Blackrock Mountain. The Blackrock orcs use it as an outer garrison.",al={"what is this place","blackrock stronghold burning steppes","what is blackrock stronghold"}},{q="Are the orcs here friendly to Thrall's Horde?",a="No. The orcs at Blackrock Stronghold belong to the Dark Horde under Rend Blackhand. They reject Thrall's leadership and are hostile to both the Alliance and Thrall's Horde.",al={"is this horde","are blackrock orcs horde","friendly to horde"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Thrall's Horde, the Blackrock clan recalls the shame of the Old Horde: bloodthirsty, corrupted remnants who reject honor and peace.",["faction:Alliance"]="The stronghold recalls the Second War. It lies within striking distance of the Kingdom of Stormwind's northern borders."},kw={"blackrock clan","blackrock stronghold","burning steppes","dark horde","rend blackhand"},rel={"zone:burningsteppes","subzone:dreadmaul-rock","topic:blackrock-clan","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Blackrock Stronghold"}}
E["subzone:dreadmaul-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Dreadmaul Rock",z="burningsteppes",s="Firegut ogres make their home among the caves and earthen mounds of Dreadmaul Rock in the Burning Steppes.",h="Firegut ogres make their home among the caves and earthen mounds of Dreadmaul Rock in the Burning Steppes.",sec={{t="Stronghold of the Firegut",b="Above the scorched plains of the Burning Steppes, Firegut ogres hold the crags and caves of Dreadmaul Rock. The massive stone formation is cut through by a labyrinthine cave system. Though its name suggests a possible tie to the Dreadmaul ogres of the Blasted Lands, the Firegut clan controls the rock.\n\nThey use its high paths, crags, and interior earthen mounds as a defended camp. From there, they dominate the surrounding wasteland and menace anyone crossing the northern slopes toward Blackrock Spire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives at Dreadmaul Rock?",a="The Firegut ogres use Dreadmaul Rock as their central base. They inhabit its outer cliff paths and the complex cave system within the rock.",al={"who is at dreadmaul rock","dreadmaul rock mobs","what ogres are at dreadmaul rock"}},{q="Why is it named Dreadmaul Rock if Firegut ogres live here?",a="The Firegut clan controls the peak, though the name suggests the rock may once have belonged to the Dreadmaul ogre clan, which has a large presence south in the Blasted Lands.",al={"why dreadmaul","dreadmaul or firegut","dreadmaul ogres connection"}},{q="What is the layout of the rock like?",a="Steep ramps wind up the crag beside an intricate cave network within, filled with ogre mounds and dwellings.",al={"dreadmaul caves","dreadmaul peak layout","navigating dreadmaul rock"}},{q="Where is Dreadmaul Rock located?",a="Dreadmaul Rock rises in the Burning Steppes, north of the path toward the Redridge Mountains and east of Blackrock Mountain.",al={"dreadmaul rock location","where is dreadmaul rock","burning steppes ogre base"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance forces guarding the border passes from Redridge, the aggressive ogres of Dreadmaul Rock are a constant, brutal hazard just across the northern ridge.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde travelers crossing the Steppes toward Blackrock Mountain must tread carefully around Dreadmaul Rock and avoid angering the territorial Firegut clan."},kw={"burning steppes","dreadmaul peak","dreadmaul rock","firegut ogres","ogre mound"},rel={"zone:burningsteppes","zone:redridge"},src={"Dreadmaul Rock"}}
E["subzone:flame-crest"] = {t="subzone",n="Flame Crest",z="burningsteppes",s="Flame Crest watches the volcanic wastes from a rocky ledge in the Burning Steppes. The neutral camp shelters scouts, beast collectors, and strategists, while wind riders carry travelers across the Redridge range and beyond.",h="Flame Crest watches the volcanic wastes from a rocky ledge in the Burning Steppes.",sec={{t="A Precarious Perch",b="Flame Crest clings to a stone ledge above the ash and lava plains. You cross a narrow wooden bridge to reach the camp. Its height helps keep prowling beasts and roaming orc warbands at bay. Wind riders carry travelers across the Redridge range to Kargath, Stonard, Thorium Point, and Rog'mar in the Riverglades.",sp=0},{t="Shadow of Blackrock",b="Scouts at Flame Crest watch the Blackrock clan entrenched in Blackrock Spire. They gather intelligence and plan how to break the renegade Dark Horde. The camp also trades with eccentric loners, including Kibler, a pet master who lives in a nearby cave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Flame Crest?",a="Flame Crest is a neutral camp in the Burning Steppes. A crude bridge leads to its narrow rocky perch, where travelers find flight routes, shelter for scouts, and supplies in a deadly region.",al={"flame crest overview","what is flame crest","burning steppes horde camp"}},{q="Where does the flight master at Flame Crest fly?",a="Wind riders from Flame Crest fly to Kargath in the Badlands, Stonard in the Swamp of Sorrows, Thorium Point in the Searing Gorge, and Rog'mar in the Riverglades.",al={"flame crest fp","flame crest flight path","where does flame crest connect"}},{q="Why is the Horde maintaining an outpost in the Burning Steppes?",a="The Horde maintains no fortress at Flame Crest. The camp is neutral, though its wind riders carry Horde travelers. From the perch, scouts watch the Blackrock clan in Blackrock Mountain. The Dark Horde defies Warchief Thrall and threatens the region, making a local vantage point matter.",al={"why is horde in burning steppes","flame crest purpose","horde mission flame crest"}},{q="Who lives in the cave at Flame Crest?",a="Kibler and his loquacious parrot, Opus, live in the cave at the back of the outcropping. Kibler is an eccentric handler interested in rare and dangerous wildlife from the surrounding wastes and Blackrock Spire.",al={"kibler cave","who is in flame crest cave","flame crest parrot"}},{q="What is Eitrigg doing at Flame Crest?",a="Eitrigg is not stationed at Flame Crest. The veteran orc serves at Warchief Thrall's side in Orgrimmar. The neutral waystation shelters traders, scouts, and wind riders who watch the Blackrock clan.",al={"eitrigg burning steppes","why is eitrigg at flame crest","ariok and eitrigg"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Flame Crest gives Horde travelers a wind rider connection and shelter in a neutral camp in the northern Burning Steppes.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc loyal to Thrall, you can watch the rogue Blackrock clan from this camp. Its presence stains the mountain."},kw={"blackrock clan","burning steppes","eitrigg","flame crest","flight path","kibler","opus","wind rider"},rel={"zone:burningsteppes","npc:eitrigg","topic:blackrock-clan","subzone:kargath","subzone:thorium-point","subzone:stonard","topic:horde"},src={"Flame Crest"}}
E["subzone:morgan-s-vigil"] = {t="subzone",n="Morgan's Vigil",z="burningsteppes",s="Alliance defenders keep watch over the passes to Blackrock Mountain from ruined Morgan's Vigil in the Burning Steppes. Charred homes and a shattered mage tower stand around their camp, the Alliance's only foothold in a land held by Dark Iron dwarves and Blackrock orcs.",h="Alliance defenders keep watch over the passes to Blackrock Mountain from ruined Morgan's Vigil in the Burning...",sec={{t="The Last Hearth in the Steppes",b="You find Morgan's Vigil on high stone above the fiery wastes of the Burning Steppes. Once a modest settlement, it fell when the horrors of the region overran it. Charred timbers and a cracked mage tower mark what remains. The defenders shelter in rough canvas tents among the soot.\n\nA gryphon roost links the camp by air to Stormwind City across the mountains. Scouts, marshals, and travelers find shelter here from the warbands below.",sp=0},{t="The Long Watch",b="Morgan's Vigil watches against the threat of Blackrock Mountain. The Dark Iron clan delves into dark sorceries, while Blackrock orcs claim the surrounding wastes. So the defenders maintain the camp's defenses and coordinate scouting runs across the ash. They also secure the vital pass leading south into Redridge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the buildings here?",a="The village's houses and other structures burned to the ground, and its mage tower crumbled. The surviving inhabitants live in tents among the ruins. No one identifies who caused the destruction.",al={"why is morgans vigil burned","ruins at morgans vigil","who destroyed morgans vigil"}},{q="Who is Morgan?",a="Morgan is the woman who gave the vigil its name. She is not among the defenders stationed at the camp now.",al={"who is morgan","morgans vigil namesake","where is morgan"}},{q="Why does the Alliance maintain this camp?",a="The Alliance keeps this camp as its only fortified vantage point in the Burning Steppes. It guards the northern pass to Redridge and watches troop movements around Blackrock Mountain. Swift supplies and reinforcements come directly from Stormwind.",al={"why alliance here","morgans vigil purpose","why keep morgans vigil"}},{q="How can I travel to and from Morgan's Vigil?",a="An Alliance gryphon master connects Morgan's Vigil directly to Stormwind City, Lakeshire, Nethergarde Keep, Thorium Point across the Searing Gorge, and Farholde Keep in the Riverglades.",al={"morgans vigil flight master","how to get to morgans vigil","flight paths morgans vigil"}},{q="Is Morgan's Vigil safe from attack?",a="Alliance sentries guard the outpost, but its perimeter remains exposed. Wandering beasts, fiery elementals, and raiding orcs lurk just beyond the ridge.",al={"is morgans vigil contested","can horde enter morgans vigil","safe zone"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you find your only safe sanctuary in the Burning Steppes on this battered bluff. Flights connect directly to Stormwind City, and defenders marshal resistance against the Dark Iron and Blackrock threats.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you know holding this ridge keeps horrors from beneath Blackrock Mountain from pouring unchecked through the pass into Redridge's vulnerable valleys and the heart of Stormwind."},kw={"alliance outpost","blackrock mountain","burning steppes","gryphon master","mage tower","morgans vigil","ruins"},rel={"zone:burningsteppes","subzone:blackrock-mountain","zone:stormwind","subzone:thorium-point","topic:alliance","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Morgan's Vigil"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-thaurissan"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Thaurissan",z="burningsteppes",s="Ash lies over the Ruins of Thaurissan in the Burning Steppes. The city once stood in the northern Redridge Mountains as the Dark Iron clan’s surface capital. During the War of the Three Hammers, Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan called Ragnaros the Firelord, and the eruption reduced the city to cinders.",h="Ash lies over the Ruins of Thaurissan in the Burning Steppes.",sec={{t="The Fall of a Kingdom",b="After High King Modimus Anvilmar died, the Dark Iron clan was exiled from Ironforge. Roughly two centuries ago, they traveled south and founded Thaurissan City. During the War of the Three Hammers, the Bronzebeard and Wildhammer clans joined forces and brought the Dark Iron to the edge of defeat.\n\nSorcerer-Thane Thaurissan sought a weapon to turn the tide. He and seven trusted sorcerers worked ancient magic deep beneath the earth. Their ritual did not summon an obedient servant. It tore open a path to the Elemental Plane and brought forth Ragnaros the Firelord. The eruption shattered the surrounding mountains, scorched the land into the Burning Steppes, raised Blackrock Mountain, and incinerated the city.",sp=0},{t="Echoes in the Ash",b="Shattered masonry and crumbled pillars lie across the wasteland. Dark Iron remnants patrol among fire elementals. The Alliance has sent expeditions to recover relics buried beneath the ash, guided by Royal Historian Archesonus in Ironforge.\n\nTouching the enchanted remnants brings vivid, terrifying memories of the cataclysm: eight dwarves chanting in despair, seven corpses sprawled around a lone kneeling thaumaturge, and a towering monolith of primal flame. That flame claimed an entire clan’s souls and freedom.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was this city before it was destroyed?",a="Before its destruction, Thaurissan City was the Dark Iron clan’s proud surface capital. They built it after exile from Ironforge, which followed the death of High King Modimus Anvilmar. The city became the center of their growing kingdom.",al={"thaurissan city lore","what was thaurissan","who built thaurissan"}},{q="How was the city destroyed?",a="Facing defeat in the War of the Three Hammers, Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan tried to summon a powerful supernatural minion. His ritual called Ragnaros the Firelord from beneath the earth. The Firelord’s arrival raised an apocalyptic volcano that reduced the city and surrounding valleys to charred ruins.",al={"how did thaurissan burn","what destroyed thaurissan","who destroyed thaurissan"}},{q="Why is the ground around the ruins an ashen wasteland?",a="The land was once the fertile northern reaches of the Redridge Mountains. Ragnaros’s summoning ruptured the earth, raised Blackrock Mountain, and scorched the expanse into an ashen wasteland.",al={"why is burning steppes ash","what happened to the land here","redridge mountains connection"}},{q="Where did the surviving Dark Iron dwarves go?",a="Ragnaros and his elemental minions enslaved the surviving Dark Iron dwarves. They went deep beneath Blackrock Mountain to build Shadowforge City. Their ruined capital lay behind as they toiled in service to the Firelord.",al={"where are the dark irons now","shadowforge city origin"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Ironforge, these ruins recall the Dark Iron clan’s hubris during the War of the Three Hammers. They remember the terrible price of calling upon elemental powers.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts and researchers, sent by Royal Historian Archesonus of Ironforge, search the ruined foundations for relics. They seek the truth about Blackrock Mountain’s master."},kw={"archesonus","burning steppes","dark iron","ragnaros","ruins of thaurissan","sorcerer-thane","thaurissan","war of the three hammers"},rel={"subzone:blackrock-mountain","topic:dark-iron-clan","topic:dark-iron-dwarf","zone:burningsteppes","npc:royal-historian-archesonus","zone:redridge","zone:ironforge","subzone:cauldron"},src={"Ruins of Thaurissan"}}
E["subzone:slither-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Slither Rock",z="burningsteppes",s="Cyrus Therepentous keeps to Slither Rock in the far northeastern cliffs of the Burning Steppes. Beyond the perilous Terror Wing Path, the cave is his solitary refuge, and his sharp tongue masks an agenda of his own.",h="Cyrus Therepentous keeps to Slither Rock in the far northeastern cliffs of the Burning Steppes.",sec={{t="A Secluded Cavern",b="Beyond the Terror Wing Path, Slither Rock lies among the scorched crags of the Burning Steppes. Far from Blackrock Spire's roaring forges and marching orc warbands, this remote hollow shelters Cyrus Therepentous, a solitary black dragonspawn.\n\nDragonspawn usually serve the Black Dragonflight with fierce loyalty, but Cyrus keeps apart from his kin. He speaks with mortal travelers instead of killing them on sight. Yet every exchange brings an insult.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Slither Rock located?",a="Slither Rock lies in the far northeastern corner of the Burning Steppes. To reach it, travelers must pass the black dragonkin patrolling the Terror Wing Path.",al={"slither rock location","where is slither rock","find slither rock"}},{q="Who lives in Slither Rock?",a="Cyrus Therepentous, a solitary black dragonspawn, lives in the cave. Unlike most of his kin, he speaks with outsiders instead of attacking at once, though his temper is foul and his words derisive.",al={"who is in slither rock","slither rock mob","slither rock npc"}},{q="Why would an adventurer seek out this cave?",a="Adventurers brave the perilous Terror Wing Path to seek Cyrus Therepentous's counsel and aid. Despite his abrasive manner, he helps them vanquish a common foe, with rude and derisive comments along the way.",al={"why go to slither rock","slither rock quests","cyrus purpose"}}},kw={"black dragonspawn","burning steppes","cyrus therepentous","slither rock","terror wing path"},rel={"npc:cyrus-therepentous","zone:burningsteppes","subzone:terror-wing-path"},src={"Slither Rock"}}
E["subzone:terror-wing-path"] = {t="subzone",n="Terror Wing Path",z="burningsteppes",s="Black dragonflight whelps and dragonkin patrol Terror Wing Path in the eastern Burning Steppes. The rocky canyon is a dangerous route to the region’s remote northeastern corner.",h="Black dragonflight whelps and dragonkin patrol Terror Wing Path in the eastern Burning Steppes.",sec={{t="A Dragonkin Roost",b="Black dragonflight broods prowl Terror Wing Path’s ash-covered foothills. They guard their clutches and hunt anything that enters the canyon. Ash and soot coat the trails beneath its craggy walls, making the passage treacherous.",sp=0},{t="A Perilous Passage",b="Black drakes patrol the valley, and the rare magma giant Volchan sometimes wanders through. Few adventurers risk the journey alone. This path is the only way to reach Slither Rock, a hidden cave in the far northeastern corner of the Steppes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures live in Terror Wing Path?",a="Whelps, broodlings, and larger dragonkin of the black dragonflight infest Terror Wing Path. They patrol the slopes and hunt ground prey across the eastern pass.",al={"terror wing mobs","what is here","dragonkin terror wing"}},{q="Where does Terror Wing Path lead?",a="Terror Wing Path winds through the eastern Burning Steppes to the remote northeastern corner. There, the hidden cave of Slither Rock lies.",al={"where does terror wing go","terror wing path route","terror wing directions"}},{q="Why is the black dragonflight active in this canyon?",a="Under Blackrock Mountain, the black dragonflight holds a strong grip over the Burning Steppes. Terror Wing Path gives the flight nesting grounds and hunting terrain. It also guards the mountain’s eastern flanks.",al={"why are dragons here","black dragonflight terror wing","dragonflight presence"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can test your aim against flying whelps and track draconic beasts through the steep canyon terrain."},kw={"black dragonflight","burning steppes","dragonkin","redridge pass","terror wing path","whelps"},rel={"zone:burningsteppes","topic:black-dragonflight","zone:redridge"},src={"Terror Wing Path"}}
E["zone:burningsteppes"] = {t="zone",n="Burning Steppes",z="burningsteppes",s="At Blackrock Mountain’s southern base, fire and lava have scorched the Burning Steppes. The land holds the main overland passage between Stormwind and Khaz Modan, where hostile clans and dragons threaten travelers.",h="At Blackrock Mountain’s southern base, fire and lava have scorched the Burning Steppes.",sec={{t="A Cataclysmic Origin",b="The Burning Steppes were once the northern reaches of the Redridge Mountains. Centuries ago, during the War of the Three Hammers, the exiled Dark Iron clan built Thaurissan as its capital here. Facing defeat by the Bronzebeard and Wildhammer clans, Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan tried to summon elemental forces.\n\nHis spell shattered the surrounding mountains and brought Ragnaros the Firelord into Azeroth. Rivers of lava opened, and Blackrock Mountain rose from the earth. The blast left the steppes charred and barren.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Second War",b="During the Second War, Blackrock Spire became the Old Horde’s foremost seat of power. Near the war’s end, the Grand Alliance of Lordaeron marched into the Burning Steppes and laid siege to the mountain. At its foot, Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer struck down Lord Anduin Lothar.\n\nLothar’s death spurred the Allied armies to rout the orcs and win the war. Ash and rusted steel still mark the valley where the battle was fought.",sp=0},{t="A Den of Monsters and Dragons",b="Blackrock orcs remain in the steppes, keeping the Old Horde’s cruelty despite Thrall’s New Horde in distant Kalimdor. From Blackrock Stronghold, they ally with the black dragonflight and Firegut ogres. They honor no truce.\n\nDark Iron dwarves and elemental servitors haunt the fiery ruins. Black drakes and wyrmkin prey on travelers crossing between Stormwind and the northern kingdoms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the ground charred and covered in lava?",a="Centuries ago, Dark Iron Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan tried to summon an elemental minion to save his clan from defeat in the War of the Three Hammers. His spell breached the Elemental Plane by mistake and summoned Ragnaros the Firelord. The blast tore open the earth, raised Blackrock Mountain, and scorched the northern Redridge Mountains.",al={"why is it burning","what happened to burning steppes","why is blackrock mountain a volcano"}},{q="Do the orcs here belong to Thrall's Horde?",a="No. The Burning Steppes’ Blackrock orcs refuse to join Thrall’s New Horde. They honor no armistice with the Alliance and keep the savage, warmongering traditions of the First and Second Wars. They serve Blackrock Spire and the black dragonflight.",al={"are these thralls orcs","are blackrock orcs horde","why are orcs hostile here"}},{q="Where did Anduin Lothar die?",a="Near the end of the Second War, Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer slew Anduin Lothar at the foot of Blackrock Mountain in the Burning Steppes. Lothar’s death drove his second-in-command, Turalyon, and the Alliance forces into a counterattack that broke the Horde’s lines.",al={"where was lothar killed","lothar death location","orgrim doomhammer and lothar duel"}},{q="Where can the Alliance find shelter in the steppes?",a="Alliance soldiers and travelers take shelter at Morgan’s Vigil, an elevated outpost in the zone’s southeastern foothills. Marshal Maxwell commands it, watches the northern pass, and monitors enemy troop movements around the mountain.",al={"alliance base burning steppes","where is alliance flight path","morgans vigil location"}},{q="Where does the Horde stage operations here?",a="Horde adventurers report to Flame Crest, an elevated camp on the northeastern ridge. Its emissaries watch the rival Blackrock clan and maintain flight connections to the Badlands, the Swamp of Sorrows, Searing Gorge, and the Riverglades.",al={"horde base burning steppes","flame crest","where is horde town"}},{q="What are the Ruins of Thaurissan?",a="The Ruins of Thaurissan are what remains of the grand city the Dark Iron clan built after its exile from Ironforge. When Thane Thaurissan summoned Ragnaros, the elemental blast destroyed his capital and bound the survivors to the Firelord’s will.",al={"thaurissan ruins","what is the destroyed dwarf city","ruins in middle of map"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you enter a somber and dangerous frontier where Supreme Commander Anduin Lothar fell. Marshal Maxwell at Morgan’s Vigil seeks brave champions against threats pressing toward Redridge.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of Thrall’s New Horde, you know Flame Crest watches the dangerous, unrepentant Blackrock clan with deep concern. Their warmongering stains the honor of orckind.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the stones of the steppes mark the Dark Iron clan’s folly during the War of the Three Hammers. Their capital was shattered, and Ragnaros was summoned.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can find rare minerals in this volcanic land, including rich thorium and Dark Iron deposits. The steppes are among the few open-air regions on Azeroth where Dark Iron can be harvested."},kw={"anduin lothar","blackrock clan","blackrock mountain","blackrock spire","burning steppes","doomhammer","flame crest","morgan's vigil","ragnaros","thaurissan"},rel={"subzone:blackrock-mountain","topic:anduin-lothar","subzone:morgan-s-vigil","subzone:flame-crest","subzone:ruins-of-thaurissan","zone:searinggorge","zone:redridge"},src={"Burning Steppes (Classic)","Burning Steppes"}}
